column3:
Radius:
Hoh-hoh-hoh! You're not even close! 
Don't be trusting in your HIT%
too much there, boy!{bpage}
As long as it's not 100%, 
you still run the risk of 
missing continuously!{bpage}
Sometimes it pays to muster up the courage 
to use Strong(2) and Fierce(3) attacks 
straight from the start, too!{mend}

Radius:
Next, let's check out the use of Elements.{bpage}
When you use an Element, the color of 
that Element's attribute remains on the battlefield 
in the form of the “Field Effect.”{bpage}
Each time you consecutively use 
the same color Element, the effectiveness of 
that colored Element group increases.{bpage}
Here, I'll show you...{wait(5)} Let's fill up all 
the Field Effect attributes with the color blue. 
Try using a blue Element after me...{mend}

Radius:
First, you've got to choose “Attack” to do 
some physical damage to your opponent 
in order to get started.{bpage}
Weak(1), Strong(2), and Fierce(3) attacks 
each add 1, 2, or 3 points to your 
Element Power Level.{bpage}
Your current level is the number that 
appears above the “Lv” symbol under 
your name there.{bpage}
Oh, I nearly forgot to tell you -- you won't 
accumulate any power unless you actually 
succeed in hitting your opponent.{bpage}
So be careful! You can't afford to miss!{mend}

Radius:
Discharging this accumulated power is what 
using Elements is all about!{bpage}
Once you've built up some power, 
you will be able to choose 
the “Element” option from the battle menu.{bpage}
When you select the Element option, gray-colored
rectangular plates appear on the screen, 
don't they?{bpage}
Those plates are the Elements you
currently have allocated.{mend}

Radius:
So...why don't you try using one of those 
blue Elements you have there, boy?{bpage}
Relax! They won't disappear when
you use them. You just won't be able to 
use them again for the rest of this battle, 
that's all!{bpage}
Once you enter another battle, you'll be able to 
use them again. So don't hold back now.{bpage}
But even though I say this, I still have to stress 
that you've got to consider the appropriate
time to use your Elements.{bpage}
Otherwise, you'll never be able to beat some of 
the harder enemies you're bound to meet! 
You've got to form the proper strategy, boy!{mend}

Radius:
Oh, but wait -- I'm forgetting something 
important. (It must be my old age.){bpage}
There are some Elements that disappear 
in a puff of smoke each time you use them. 
The Element “αTablet” is just one example!{bpage}
These are called “Consumable Elements,” and 
they have the symbol “α” in front of their names. 
These don't regenerate after each battle.{bpage}
However, the benefit of such 
Consumable Elements is that you can allocate up 
to five of them to the same Element Grid space.{bpage}
Doing so allows you to use several of them in 
the same battle, unlike Basic Elements, 
which normally can only be used once in any one battle.{bpage}
That is why Consumable Elements also
have a number such as “x5” after
their names. That's the number you
currently hold in that Grid position.{bpage}
This number will decrease as the
Elements are used.
However, after each battle, you can
restock more to use next time.{mend}

Radius:
Anyway, enough about that.
More about actually using Elements...{bpage}
I'm sure you'll notice that each
time you use an Element, your
Element Power Level (as shown by
the “Lv” number) will go down.{bpage}
It's just simple subtraction, really.{bpage}
For instance, say you're currently
at Lv 3 and you decide to use a
“αTablet” Element allocated at
Lv 1 in your Element Grid.{bpage}
In this case, 3 minus 1 leaves 2.
So your current Element Power Level
will now be changed to Lv 2.{bpage}
You can use Elements anytime, so long
as your Stamina value is above 1.0.{bpage}
So in this case, you'll still be
able to use Elements with a Power 
Level of up to Lv 2 right
after using the “αTablet” Element!{mend}

Radius:
What's this? You still haven't managed to turn 
all the Field Effect attributes blue yet?{bpage}
What, you expect an old man to do everything 
for you? You slacker! Anyway, here we go...{mend}

Radius:
Hoh-hoh-hoh!
Was that too much for you?
Sorry about that, young'un!{bpage}
Conversely, when there is a lot of blue in 
the Field Effect attributes, the Elements of 
the opposite color -- red -- will be weakened.{bpage}
So try to discern your enemy's attack pattern 
and fill the Field with the opposite color of his
attacks as a form of defense.{bpage}
This strategy of using Elements is sure to come 
in handy, so put it to good use, sonny!{mend}

Radius:
Hoh-hoh-hoh... How was that?
You learn something there, boy?{bpage}
Anyway, I guess it's time to 
bring this lesson to an end.
Here you go... Hah!{mend}

Radius:
Huh?
You've grown mighty strong since 
the last time I fought you!{bpage}
If that's how it is then, try this for size, young'un!
This'll teach you to respect your elders... Hah!{mend}

Radius:
Ho-ho-houch! 
I'm getting tired more easily in my old age!{bpage}
But nonetheless, well done there, young'un!
You're quite proficient now...{wait(30)}
thanks to my tutoring!{mend}

Radius:
Ho-ho-houch! 
I'm getting tired more easily in my old age!{bpage}
But nonetheless, well done there, young'un!
You're quite proficient now...{wait(30)}
thanks to my tutoring!{mend}

Karsh:
Right! That does it!{bpage}
Quick, attack him with the opposite 
Element attribute color...
        BLACK!        {mend}

Karsh:
You nincompoop! You should always carry
Elements of every color!{bpage}
Then how about you there...?{mend}

Peppor:
I'm shakin' in my shoes to tell you this, sir, 
but I don't have any either!{bpage}
We'll have to let you, Sir Karsh, 
show us how it's done...{mend}

Karsh:
!?
Useless fools!{bpage}
Err......{bpage}
Real men don't need magic when 
they can fight with their might!{mend}

Peppor:
That was no BLACK ATTACK
Element you used just now!{bpage}
It was a Black Element that makes your foe 
MORE SUSCEPTIBLE TO attacks of the opposite
color attribute, WHITE, wasn't it!?{mend}

Peppor:
You DID bring a WHITE ATTACK Element 
with you, didn't you!?{bpage}
If you didn't bring one with you, 
you're more stupid than I thought!{mend}

Solt:
Err......{bpage}
How awfully awful! 
I'm afraid I didn't, Peppor...{mend}

Peppor:
It's them again... those tough guys!{bpage}
You said you brought a shakingly awesome 
Element with you, didn't you?{mend}

Solt:
I have a brilliantly brilliant Element
this time, Peppor.{bpage}
It's a new... Summoning Element!{mend}

Peppor:
Shaking!!! It sure sounds good.{bpage}
Well then, shake a leg! 
Hurry up and use it on these smart alecks!{mend}

Peppor:
Huh?
Nothing happened!{bpage}
I wonder what went wrong...{mend}

Solt:
Ah......
I forgetfully forgot!{bpage}
You can't use a Summoning Element 
until all the Field Effect attributes are 
the same color!{mend}

Peppor:
......
You muddle-head!{bpage}
Well then -- hurry up and turn all the Field Effect
attributes the same color and try again!{mend}

Solt:
But Peppor...{bpage}
You can't use the same Element twice 
in the same battle! 
Any foolish fool knows that!{mend}

Peppor:
...............
...............{bpage}
Oh my god, Solt! 
Can't you ever do anything right?{mend}

ZOAH:
...............
...............
...............{bpage}
ARE YOU CLOWNS FINISHED WITH YOUR
COMEDY ACT YET?{mend}

Peppor:
The nerve of these guys!
Thinking they can storm our front gate!{bpage}
This time we ought to give them the shaking
they deserve!{mend}

Peppor:
Today we brought along
a helping hand!{bpage}
He's tough! He's mean!
And he's really, really big, too!{bpage}
Show them what you can do!!!{bpage}
......{wait(90)}
I said show them what you can do!{wait(90)}
......{bpage}
Yoo~hoo~!{wait(60)} Oh, Ketcho~p!{wait(60)}
Come out, come out, wherever you are!{mend}

Peppor:
Ooooohhh! You see...
My, my! Aren't we strong now?{bpage}
This time we're going to beat you for sure!!!{mend}

Solt:
Go! Go! Ketchop!!!{bpage}
Try out your special 
Karate Ket-Chop on them!{mend}

Solt:
Well...{bpage}
I thought that we all wouldn't get to see 
how fiercely fierce Ketchop was if they 
were all passed out!{mend}

Peppor:
.........{bpage}
Have you got your priorities straight!?{bpage}
Doesn't that defeat our whole purpose!?{bpage}
Do it again, and you're shaken dead meat,
Solt!{mend}

Peppor:
This doesn't look good!
We could be shaken here...{bpage}
Hey! Ketchop! Why don't you shaking
well do something?{mend}

Beeba:
Ah!{wait(10)} No more friend come...?{wait(60)}
Beeba no friend left...{wait(60)}
I beebary lonely now...{wend(60)}

Criosphinx:
Nigra in candida vertere.
Here be an easy one to start off with!{bpage}
What the extorted one is bled...
With knuckles of fear...
The plumage of a coward when...
Faced with the hottest of heat...{bpage}
Answer my question! 
What is it I be?{mend}

Criosphinx:
Dimidium facti qui bene coepit habet.
Well begun is half done.
Now, here my second riddle be...{bpage}
Auburn less the burn...
Iron pyrite less the fool...
All that glitters is not thus...
Though silence is...{bpage}
Answer my question!
What is it I be?{mend}

Criosphinx:
Now riddle number three! 
Bene rem gere!{bpage}
In my anger, I see...
Both the rag to charge at...
And the flag to stop at...
Blushing, I walk the royal carpet...{bpage}
Answer my question!
What is it I be?{mend}

Criosphinx:
Thou art quick on the uptake!
Question four... Accipe!{bpage}
It isn't easy being...
A friend of the planet...
With the jealous monster's eyes...
Giving me a sign to proceed!{bpage}
Answer my question!
What is it I be?{mend}

Criosphinx:
Velim tibi ita persuadeas.
Just two more to go!{bpage}
Mare et caelum et viola!
Give me a melancholy gloom...
But a first prize ribbon...
Makes me feel I've royal blood!{bpage}
Answer my question!
What is it I be?{mend}

Criosphinx:
Usus est magister optimus.
By deduction alone ye should
my answer already know...{bpage}
Like pontoon less the knave...
Or Jolly Roger less the bones...
Even the top rank of self-defense...
Is no protection from the Plague!{bpage}
Answer my question!
What is it I be?{mend}

Mysterious Monster:
Quid me vis? I am the Criosphinx.
And thou hast trespassed on my domain!{bpage}
Why must thou turmoil unto this land bring?
Then turmoil I bring unto thee!
Depending on how thou meet this trial,
thou may be allowed to leave this place alive!{bpage}
This be an island which no man 
hath visited for aeons.
The Criosphinx has grown quite bored...{bpage}
If thou possessest the courage
to match thy wits to mine,
thy sins may be forgiven when thou answer 
correctly my questions six!{bpage}
Now riddle me this...{mend}

Criosphinx:
Quid est? Quidnam tu hominis es?{bpage}
What? Thou sayest thou canst
not answer my question?
Male factum!{bpage}
Then what have I to do with thee?
Begone from my sight!
Abi in malem rem!{mend}

Criosphinx:
Quid ais?
Mira narras!{bpage}
Impressive! Ne'er thought I there'd be
humans who could defeat the
Criosphinx by force alone!{bpage}
Thy way of life intrigues me!
To conquer all obstacles with
brawn rather than brain...{wait(30)}
.........{bpage}
But I warn ye, woes shalt surely 
befall one such as thee!{mend}

Criosphinx:
Sat prata biberunt!
Gratulor felicitati tuae!{bpage}
Well done! Thou hast solved all of my riddles!{bpage}
Thy brains art as impressive as thy brawn!{mend}

Bene vale! Bene valeto!
Always be diligent in thy practice!{bpage}
Me tibi commendo! Vale!
I take my leave of thee! Farewell!{mend}

Solt:
This time we shall not be beaten!{bpage}
I shall blow them to pieces with one of those 
powerfully powerful Elements you bought me,
Peppor!{mend}

Solt:
How tragically tragic!!!
I hate to tell you this, Peppor, but...{bpage}
I just remembered that I lost 
the Summoning Element I had with me!{mend}

Peppor:
......!?
What do you mean, you “lost” it?{bpage}
Don't tell me you dropped it or your dog ate 
it or some other stupid excuse like that!{bpage}
You're asking for a darn good shaking!{mend}

Solt:
I'm not that stupidly
stupid, you know, Peppor!{bpage}
Actually, if you must know...
that centipede monster in the
Hydra Marshes stole it from me!{bpage}
And I was enjoying that excitingly exciting
expedition up till then, too...{mend}

Peppor:
What do you mean, a centipede
monster stole your Element???{bpage}
What, he snuck up behind you and picked 
all your pockets with his hundreds of 
legs or something!?{mend}

Solt:
No, Peppor.{bpage}
When I say stole, I don't mean he picked 
my pockets or anything like that!{bpage}
I mean he took it from me by laying a 
Trap Element in which my Element got caught!{mend}

Peppor:
What in spice's name are you talking about?{bpage}
Would you kindly explain to me what a shaking 
Trap Element is?{mend}

Solt:
Well...{wait(10)}
Errr...{bpage}
It's difficultly difficult to explain in words, 
Peppor, so I will give you a demonstration.{bpage}
I will lay a Trap in front of you, Peppor, 
and then get you to use one of 
your special Elements.{mend}

Solt:
Now, you see how I took 
your Element there, Peppor?{bpage}
I used a Trap Element designed exclusively 
to capture “Black Hole” Elements!{bpage}
You see, each Trap Element only works 
on one kind of Element.{bpage}
They can't capture any Elements other 
than the ones they were designed to capture!{mend}

Peppor:
Shaking!{wait(10)}
Hmm...{bpage}
I see what you mean about having your 
Summoning Element stolen there...{bpage}
Alright, now I understand.{wait(10)}
So you can give me back my
Black Hole Element now!{mend}

Peppor:
Huh......?{bpage}
Well, I guess it doesn't matter, seeing as 
you've got your hands on it now...{bpage}
So...{wait(10)}why don't you hurry on up 
and use that Element you just trapped 
on the enemy!{bpage}
Come on! What are you waiting for?{bpage}
Huh......?{mend}

Solt:
You know you can't use an Element until 
you have equipped it properly!{bpage}
So we'll have to wait until after this battle is 
over before we can re-equip it and use it!{bpage}
......{wait(20)}
Oops!{mend}

Peppor:
...{wait(120)}WH-{wait(120)}WH-{wait(110)}WH-{wait(100)}WH-{wait(90)}WH-{wait(80)}WH-{wait(70)}WH-{wait(60)}WH-{wait(50)}WH-
{wait(40)}WH-{wait(30)}WH-{wait(20)}WH-{wait(15)}WH-{wait(10)}WH-{wait(5)}WH-{wait(1)}WH-{wait(1)}WH-{wait(1)}WH-{wait(1)}WH-
WHAT DID YOU JUST SAY!?!{bpage}
WHY THE HELL DO YOU ALWAYS
HAVE TO BE SO DAMNED STUPID?{bpage}
THAT DOES IT!!!{wait(10)}
YOU'RE IN FOR A REAL SHAKING NOW!{mend}

Katsuhisa Higuchi:
Hello, people! I'm Katsuhisa, 
and I'm a programmer.{bpage}
Unlike the artists, musicians, 
and scenario writers, etc., we programmers 
don't stand out that much, I guess.{bpage}
So today I thought I'd teach you folks just
what a program is!{bpage}
Hold on while I call some of my friends!{bpage}
Heeeey yooouuu guuuuuysss!!!!{mend}

Katsuhisa Higuchi:
Kazumi programmed the sections that display 
and maneuver polygon models.{bpage}
Why don't you show 'em, Kazumi?{mend}

Katsuhisa Higuchi:
Miya wrote the program sections that 
manipulate effects.{bpage}
His effects look like this...{mend}

Kohji Ohno:
OHNO!!!{wait(30)}
No, I'm not in trouble{wait(10)}
...that's my name!{mend}

Katsuhisa Higuchi:
He coded the special effects used in the battles,
as well as the menu system.{bpage}
Go for it, Ohno!{mend}

Katsuhisa Higuchi:
Oh, and as for me...{wait(5)}
Well, I was responsible for the overall battle
programming.{bpage}
Why, I even wrote the data and 
functions that allow this image of me 
to talk to you like this!{bpage}
The artificial intelligence and logic of 
the monsters and other enemies was 
also written by yours truly.{mend}

Katsuhisa Higuchi:
Thanks for listening to my long speech here.{bpage}
Oh, and I really appreciate that you bought 
a copy of Chrono Cross, too!{bpage}
Well, until we meet again in some other game, 
take care and...{bpage}
SA~YO~NA~RA~~~!{mend}
